The attached image illustrates the adjuvant effect of Nano-11 nanoparticles on antibody responses. It presents anti-recombinant protective antigen (rPA) IgG titers in mice immunized with rPA alone or formulated with aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 at different doses. Nano-11, at doses of 200 and 50 µg, significantly enhanced antibody titers, showing similar or superior efficacy compared to AH. Even at the lowest dose of 12.5 µg, Nano-11 significantly boosted antibody titers above rPA alone. These results demonstrate Nano-11's strong ability to augment the humoral immune response to vaccine antigens.